---
// The pieces of one album of the ill-tempered week, each with its player and its score (2026-11-14). The front page
// shows the newest complete album with it and every album's own page shows its album with it, so the two cannot
// drift. Everything is read from the album's record; the links come from the committed day files it names.
import OverlookedScore from '@/components/ill-tempered-week/OverlookedScore'
import TurnScore from '@/components/ill-tempered-week/TurnScore'
import UnisonScore from '@/components/ill-tempered-week/UnisonScore'
import { clock, weekday, type Album } from '@/lib/ill-tempered-week/albums'
import { HINT, overlookedLinks, turnSaidLink as saidLink, unisonLinks, warSignals } from '@/lib/ill-tempered-week/pages'
import { dayShort, mmss } from '@/lib/ill-tempered-week/score'
import { FORM as OV } from '@/lib/ill-tempered-week/score-overlooked'
import { FORM as UN } from '@/lib/ill-tempered-week/score-unison'

interface Props {
  album: Album
}

const { album } = Astro.props
const link = 'underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-fg'
const pct = (x: number): string => `${Math.round(100 * x)} %`
const o = album.pieces.overlooked
const u = album.pieces.unison
const t = album.pieces.turn
const turnDay = t?.days.find((d) => d.turn)
// The days before the last that stayed a cluster (the last day never takes the chord, by the piece's rule).
const clusters = u ? u.days.slice(0, -1).filter((d) => !d.peak).length : 0
const most = u ? u.days.reduce((a, b) => (b.agreement > a.agreement ? b : a)) : null
const signals = u ? warSignals(u) : []
const turnSaidLink = t ? saidLink(t) : null
const hint = HINT
---

<section id="overlooked" class="itw-piece mb-16" aria-label="Overlooked">
  <p class="kicker mb-1">I · chamber ensemble</p>
  <h2 class="itw-title">Overlooked</h2>
  <audio id="itw-audio-overlooked" class="itw-player mt-3" controls preload="metadata" src={o.audio}></audio>
  <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">
    {clock(o.seconds)} · {album.complete ? 'seven days' : `edition ${o.edition} of 7, to ${weekday(o.newest_day)}`} ·
    <a class={link} href={o.audio} download>download</a> · CC BY 4.0
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
    Each day, the headline that drew the least attention on its own platform, among all thirteen fields and from a field not heard
    before that week, is said once. The instrument of its field answers with the headline’s own speech melody, in the rhythm it was
    spoken; then the melody becomes a motif, and violins, violas, piano, cellos and basses take it up. Earlier days keep sounding,
    {' '}{OV.dbPerDay} dB softer for each day of age, so the overlooked gather into a polyphony across the week, while the day’s most
    attended headlines murmur underneath. A motif ends with its day if the newest day no longer names its field. At the end of
    the newest day everything still kept sounds at once; then a cut, and the first day’s headline once more, alone.
  </p>
  <OverlookedScore
    client:idle
    record={o}
    links={overlookedLinks(o)}
    audioId="itw-audio-overlooked"
    id="itw-score-overlooked"
    label={`The score of Overlooked, ${album.title}: one lane per voice, time from left to right.`}
    hint={hint}
  />
</section>

{u && most && (
  <section id="unison" class="itw-piece mb-16" aria-label="Unison">
    <p class="kicker mb-1">II · string orchestra, brass, timpani</p>
    <h2 class="itw-title">Unison</h2>
    <audio id="itw-audio-unison" class="itw-player mt-3" controls preload="metadata" src={u.audio}></audio>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">
      {clock(u.seconds)} · war and violence · <a class={link} href={u.audio} download>download</a> · CC BY 4.0
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
      Every signal that named war and violence is one string glissando: its section by the attention it drew on its platform, the
      most attended highest, its first pitch from its own headline as spoken, its entry at the hour it was published, where its
      platform gives one. Each day the whole
      mass glides towards A’s harmonic chord exactly as far as the press agreed: the share of the day’s war signals naming its most named
      story. Where at least {pct(UN.threshold)} agreed, brass and timpani take up the chord and the day’s most attended headline is said
      over it. Every day, a solo double bass then plays the speech melody of the day’s least attended war headline, outside the chord.
      The press agreed most on {weekday(most.day)}, {pct(most.agreement)} on {most.story};
      {clusters === 0 ? ' every day before the last reached the chord, and the last never takes it.' : ` ${clusters} day${clusters === 1 ? '' : 's'} before the last stayed a cluster, and the last never takes the chord.`}
    </p>
    <UnisonScore
      client:idle
      record={u}
      week={album.week}
      links={unisonLinks(u)}
      audioId="itw-audio-unison"
      id="itw-score-unison"
      label={`The score of Unison, ${album.title}: every war signal as a glissando, pitch upwards, time from left to right.`}
      hint={hint}
    />
    <details class="dv-table-fallback mt-6">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">Every war signal of the week, with its link ({signals.length})</summary>
      <div class="itw-table-wrap mt-3">
        <table class="itw-table">
          <caption class="sr-only">Every war signal of {album.title}: when it enters, its section, its attention, its glissando and its headline</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">enters</th><th scope="col">day</th><th scope="col">section</th><th scope="col">attention</th><th scope="col">glide (Hz)</th><th scope="col">headline</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {signals.map((s) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="num">{mmss(s.at_s)}</td>
                <td class="num">{dayShort(s.day)}</td>
                <td>{s.section}{s.tremolo ? ', trem.' : ''}</td>
                <td class="num">{pct(s.attention)}</td>
                <td class="num">{Math.round(s.from_hz)} → {Math.round(s.to_hz)}</td>
                <td>{s.href ? <a class="itw-link" href={s.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.text}</a> : s.text}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
)}

{t && (
  <section id="turn" class="itw-piece mb-16" aria-label="Turn">
    <p class="kicker mb-1">III · electronics</p>
    <h2 class="itw-title">Turn</h2>
    <audio id="itw-audio-turn" class="itw-player mt-3" controls preload="metadata" src={t.audio}></audio>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">
      {clock(t.seconds)} · AI and its harms · <a class={link} href={t.audio} download>download</a> · CC BY 4.0
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
      A rhythmicon of the platform families: each pulses as many beats a bar as its harmonic number (search 5, news 6, social 7,
      tech 9) and sings its vowel on that harmonic of A; how many of its beats sound is its count of AI signals that day, so the
      bar fills as attention does. Busy days run faster. {turnDay
        ? <>The week turned on {weekday(turnDay.day)}, with {turnDay.signals} signals: one bar sounds every beat of every family, and a silent bar carries the day’s most attended AI headline, “{turnDay.said}”.</>
        : <>This week did not turn.</>}
    </p>
    <TurnScore
      client:idle
      record={t}
      week={album.week}
      saidLink={turnSaidLink}
      audioId="itw-audio-turn"
      id="itw-score-turn"
      label={`The score of Turn, ${album.title}: one row per platform family, one cell per bar, time from left to right.`}
      hint={hint}
    />
  </section>
)}
